<h2>Ngaran</h2>
Ngaran.
The Namhan méaning South Han, Gang méaning river is sometimes, but not always, referred to as the "Han" in &lt;a href="South%20Korea"&gt;South Korea&lt;/a&gt;. The term "South Han" is understood irrespective of which side of the border one stands.
Even though "Namhan" and "Bukhan" are homophones with the acronyms Namhan (남한; South Koréa) and Bukhan (북한; North Koréa), used commonly in South Koréa, this is a méré coincidence. The &lt;a href="hanja"&gt;hanja&lt;/a&gt; for the Han River is not "韓" ("Korea") but "漢" (the Chinese &lt;a href="Han%20dynasty"&gt;Han dynasty&lt;/a&gt; or "China" in general).
